aura_consensus::baseline surveys the six consensus layers (proposer,
block-signature, QC, finality, validator set, VRF leader) and classifies
each as placeholder — 0 implemented, 6 placeholders, 0 missing. The
aura-consensus binary refuses to pretend consensus exists: no arguments
→ exit 2 with every missing capability and its phase; unknown command →
exit 64; report exits 3 on a non-workspace.

- tools/gen_b0_vectors.py pins the survey in b0_baseline.txt
- tools/nc_b0.py — 6 negative controls, each reddening a named test
- tools/write_b0_evidence.py — gates, report, inventory, SHA256SUMS
- D0 test renamed: the_four_unlanded_layers → the_unlanded_layers
- CHANGELOG entry, CONSENSUS_PLAN.md receipt, docs/NODE.md + STATUS.md
- audit_closeout.py: CONSENSUS_PHASES=[B0], CURRENT=B0, EXPECTED_TOTAL_NC=177

Gates: 10 unit tests, D0 13/13, D1 12/12, 6/6 NC, make test ALL GREEN
